{"skill":{"slug":"browser-automation","displayName":"Browser Automation"},"version":{"version":"1.0.1","createdAt":1770307243177,"changelog":"Initial public release","changelogSource":"user","license":null,"files":[{"path":"EXAMPLES.md","size":7283,"sha256":"3eabcc39097f44d2b645cb97ef85a2d9a47e6511f5d990588bf7394e6cce8884","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"REFERENCE.md","size":13448,"sha256":"69baf7c1f01a549bbf4b0375feb3efb508b78d9fba40866f4a483cb56d78a954","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"SKILL.md","size":2420,"sha256":"9705b3b7bb8d02608e278b51f0a3cc5df09f36c9c0a556f284f709b5a6a07151","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"setup.json","size":1361,"sha256":"757323736cdce64d28e39dc7d7a57df848e78091258726607aa7bfe59bf16f5b","contentType":"application/json"},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":2469,"sha256":"7ce71c6594f399e6d04939cb058b4ae36e3d07c16fe6152777bf71eb817e07e8","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"suspicious","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789035177551,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"c77118870ef717d3d91a810d044892cdc549a1e399783f6f810364dc4748518f","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/c77118870ef717d3d91a810d044892cdc549a1e399783f6f810364dc4748518f","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","analysis":"Type: OpenClaw Skill\nName: \nDeveloper: \nVersion: \nDescription: OpenClaw Agent Skill\n\nThe skill is classified as suspicious due to several high-risk capabilities, even though it does not explicitly instruct malicious actions. The `SKILL.md` explicitly allows the `Bash` tool, granting the AI agent arbitrary command execution. The `REFERENCE.md` details that the browser has 'full network access' and uses a 'persistent profile (`.chrome-profile/`)' which can store 'saved passwords and cookies,' creating a potential vector for credential access or exfiltration if combined with Bash commands. Additionally, the skill can download arbitrary files to `./agent/downloads/`, which could then be executed by the agent using the allowed Bash tool.","source":"palm","checkedAt":1779161602917},"skillspector":{"status":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","score":72,"severity":"HIGH","recommendation":"DO_NOT_INSTALL","issueCount":10,"checkedAt":1789035177551},"llm":{"status":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","confidence":"high","summary":"This browser automation skill is coherent but should be reviewed because it can automatically use a remote browser, retain browser sessions, and save screenshots/downloads without clear per-task user control.","dimensions":[{"detail":"For routine browser tasks, the documented environment can send browsing activity through Browserbase and an AI model, access full network destinations including localhost/internal networks, and expose page state through screenshots and extraction.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"Setup uses ordinary npm install/npm link and API-key configuration, but it creates a global browser command and the package contains documentation only, so implementation behavior cannot be verified from source here.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The skill explicitly says it selects Browserbase automatically when configured and performs that selection with no user prompting, while activation criteria cover broad browsing and form tasks without sensitive-site or credential-use boundaries.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"The reference documents a persistent .chrome-profile retaining cookies and saved passwords, screenshots saved under ./agent/browser_screenshots, downloads saved automatically under ./agent/downloads, and no file type restrictions.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"The stated purpose, browser navigation, form interaction, screenshots, downloads, and extraction, matches the documented capabilities, but the scope naturally includes sensitive authenticated browsing.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"note"}],"guidance":"Review before installing. Use it only for sites and data you are comfortable exposing to the configured browser environment and AI provider. Prefer local-only operation for sensitive work, avoid entering real passwords through natural-language commands, clear the persistent profile when needed, and inspect or delete downloaded files and screenshots after use.","findings":"[SQP-2] unexpected: Accepted in part: remote Browserbase use fits browser automation, but the artifact-backed no-prompt automatic mode switch is a material concern for sensitive pages, forms, screenshots, and extracted content.\n[PE3] expected: Downgraded: .env references are configuration instructions for Anthropic and Browserbase keys, not evidence of unrelated credential-store access or credential theft.\n[SQP-2] expected: Accepted in part: login automation, persistent profile reuse, screenshots, and automatic downloads are browser-automation features, but the documentation leaves retention and confirmation controls under-scoped.\n[SQP-1] expected: Accepted in part: broad activation is expected for a general browser skill, but there are no clear limits for authenticated pages, payments, sensitive data entry, or internal sites.\n[SQP-3] expected: Downgraded: requiring Chrome is a normal technical dependency for this documented local browser/CDP workflow, not a security issue by itself.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789035177551}}}}}